So I tried the protection racket with an archaeologist on NAO.  After 800 
1000 turns I found a 0:1 /oW in a general store on DL3.  Wished for:

3b?oC (got 1)
+3 SDSM (got +0)
+3 jumping boots (got +3)

Killed a mimic to gain a level so I could safely wish for:

+2 Grayswandir (got +2)

Then read a level 1 spellbook until it teleported me out of the shop.  I 
abandoned the pet and ran down to Minetown (bones, nothing special 
though) to gather useful items from the shops.  Went back to the main 
dungeon and went down to Sokoban and did the first level as far as the 
scrolls of earth.  I had enough HP now to safely use the wrest wish on 
the Eye.

Next was a leprechaun hall, which gave enough gold for 3 donations -- 
gated back to Minetown for that.  Proceeded down through the main 
dungeon, mostly skipping levels with the pickaxe after checking them with 
telepathy.  I did find a nice bones pile with a chock full bag of holding 
and Magicbane.

Dug down to the Castle.  It was rather tricky since I did not have 
conflict or a rubber chicken or pets or even much HP.  Eventually I won 
through though.  (T:4470)  This wand was also 0:1.  Spent it on a wand of 
polymorph, helm of brilliance, and two magic markers.  I gated back to 
Sokoban and did some polypiling.

There was rather a shortage of markers and polyfodder, so I was only able 
to reverse genocide up to level 21, and there wasn't enough to alchemize 
with.  But I had luckily found the three !oGA needed to max Int and Wis.  
Reverse genocide of tengu gave TC and teleportitis.  Genocided ;.

The rest of the game was straightforward, although I wasted many turns 
because of mistakes and forgetting to bring certain items with me.  For 
example, I jumped out of a bear trap in Gehennom and spent the final 1000 
turns with wounded legs == no more jumping.

 The replay (in only one file!) is:
http://alt.org/nethack/ttyrec/Rast/2005-06-06.17:47:45.ttyrec
If you're using Windows you probably need http://angband.pl/termrec.html 
to play it back.

My various mistakes added perhaps 2000 turns.  Of course most of the 
first 800 turns were wasted too.  With better play and ideal 
circumstances I think a 5000 turn ascension is possible.


